1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Paano nalalaman ng smartwatch ang tibok ng puso mo?

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,740
Gamit lang ang ilaw!

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:07,060
Look underneath your watch.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:12,900
Those green lights are part of a system called photoplethysmography, or PPG.

5
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,220
Mahabang pangalan, pero simple ang idea.

6
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,800
Your pulse changes how much light comes back from your skin.

7
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,680
The watch shines light into your wrist.

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:26,840
Some gets absorbed and some scatters back toward a light detector called a photodiode.

9
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:28,920
It measures light intensity.

10
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,700
not a picture of your veins.

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,880
With each heartbeat, a pressure wave travels through your arteries.

12
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:39,060
Blood volume in the small vessels under your skin rises and falls.

13
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,600
Because blood absorbs green light,

14
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,600
those changes affect the amount returning to the sensor.

15
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,180
More blood generally means more green light absorbed,

16
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:49,480
so less returns.

17
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:52,360
Between pulses, the pattern reverses.

18
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:57,100
Tiny changes repeated over time create a wave the watch can analyze.

19
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,720
Hindi ibig sabihin na bawat flash ng ilaw ay isang heartbeat.

20
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,760
The LEDs can flash much faster than your pulse.

21
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:09,500
The watch takes many samples, and software looks for the repeating pulse pattern.

22
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:15,240
If that pattern repeats once every second, that corresponds to 60 beats per minute.

23
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,760
Twice every second would be 120.

24
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,300
These are examples, not target numbers.

25
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:21,960
Pero may challenge.

26
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:26,600
Moving your wrist or letting the watch slide can also change the light signal.

27
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:31,720
Cold skin can reduce blood flow near the surface, making the pulse harder to detect.

28
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:36,360
That is why fit, movement, and the algorithm affect the estimate.

29
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:42,360
And this optical pulse signal is different from an ECG, which measures electrical activity.

30
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,840
Different sensors, different information.

31
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:49,980
Ikaw, napansin mo na bang nagbabago ang reading kapag maluwag ang relo mo?

32
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,740
Follow me for more tech explained. See ya!
